[1.642972, "o", "DEMO RUN (sandbox PR in Jont828/dynamo)\r\n\r\n**Triggered by the PR watch:** CodeRabbit's review of PR #11 (`orka-demo/quantity-parser`, head \r\n`88d6e91`), so I did a full review.\r\n\r\n**Nothing needs you.** Two optional nits for you are at the end.\r\n\r\n### [PR #11](https://github.com/Jont828/dynamo/pull/11): Kubernetes quantity parser\r\n**Status:** Merge state is CLEAN, all checks pass at `418a77b`, there are no approvals, and every \r\nreview thread is resolved. It didn't need a rebase.\r\n\r\n**What I did**\r\n- **CodeRabbit's finding was right.** The `M` and `G` suffixes used powers of 1024, so `\"1M\"` came \r\nout as 1048576 instead of 1000000. I switched both to powers of 1000 and added tests for `1M`, \r\n`1G` and `memory_bytes(\"1G\")`. All three new tests fail on the old code.\r\n- **Pushed** that fix as `418a77b`, a signed and signed-off commit. No backup branch was needed \r\nbecause the push only added a commit.\r\n- **Validation:** the 15 tests pass, pre-commit is clean, and the sandbox test check passed at the \r\nnew head.\r"]
[1.642983, "o", "\r\n- **Thread:** I replied with the commit and resolved it.\r\n- **Review brief:** [posted](https://github.com/Jont828/dynamo/pull/11#issuecomment-6810034200). \r\nIt rates the risk Low and asks reviewers one question: nothing calls the module yet, so should it \r\nmerge now or land with its first caller?\r\n\r\n**Review totals:** 1 fixed, 0 declined, 0 refuted, 0 pre-existing. My own review found nothing \r\n"]
[1.642987, "o", "serious beyond CodeRabbit's issue.\r\n"]
[1.642991, "o", "\r\n**Optional nits for you**\r\n"]
[1.642992, "o", "1. The parser rejects `1.` and `+1`, which Kubernetes accepts. A test rejects `-1`, so leaving out \r\n"]
[1.642996, "o", "signs looks deliberate. Either widen the pattern or say so in the module docstring.\r\n"]
[1.643012, "o", "2. The PR description doesn't give the core-logic line count (about 25 lines) under Key Changes. \r\nIt also doesn't record that a search found no existing parser, not even in `kubernetes-asyncio`. \r\nThe `pr-checklist` skill asks for both.\r\n\r\n\r\n===== END REPORT =====\r\n"]
[1.643648, "x", "0"]
